# Rank 1915 / CVE-2024-1023: vert.x's CombinerExecutor held its task tail in a
# per-instance netty FastThreadLocal (GHSA-5667-3wch-7q7w). A FastThreadLocal's
# constructor takes a global index from InternalThreadLocalMap.nextVariableIndex(),
# a counter that only increments, and every FastThreadLocalThread sizes its
# indexed-variables array to the largest index claimed; the slot is held for the
# life of the instance and never returned. A field initializer runs once per
# construction of the enclosing instance, so `new FastThreadLocal<>()` in a
# non-static field of a class instantiated per connection pool grows every
# event-loop thread's array without bound. The fix (dd6f6430, cited directly by
# the advisory; 665ceba3 is the identical change on the 4.4 branch) makes the
# field static -- one slot for the class -- and threads the executor identity
# through the stored value. The remediation is present at <fix> (line 46) and
# absent at <fix>^ (line 36): the discriminating fact is one keyword, static.
#
# The corpus family hint (CWE-444 body framing) does not apply: this commit
# fixes a resource leak, and the recorded CWE-119/CWE-200 does not match the
# mechanism either -- the axis is unbounded per-instance allocation, judged by
# code.UnboundedAllocationReview (VYQL-DOS-041, CWE-400/770), which is the
# concept reused here rather than minted. ThreadLocalScopeOverwriteWithoutCleanup
# is a lifecycle-overwrite race; the resource.ResourceLeak taint family needs a
# release-ordering path, and none exists: no untrusted value flows, the
# attacker's cost is the act of opening connections.
#
# The detection reads the instance_field_init token the Java walk now emits for
# a field initializer that constructs the named type, per class or per instance:
# perInstanceFastThreadLocal labels the class context of a class that
# constructs a FastThreadLocal into an instance field, and VYQL-DOS-041 judges
# it. Until that fact existed the declaration lowered to a bare assignment --
# jvModifierTokens ran for classes and methods but never for fields, and the
# class member walk skipped assignments -- so `vyql graph` was byte-identical
# across the fix and a binding on the FastThreadLocal constructor labelled the
# same single node at both revisions (1 -> 1). A text route was never a
# substitute: the vulnerable file itself declares `protected static final
# class InProgressTail`, so any "static appears near the field" heuristic
# reads the vulnerable form as patched.
#
# Measured on the real checkout (--cache off, bounded, three runs per side):
# the change-carrying pool subtree (14 files) reports 1 VYQL-DOS-041 high on
# CombinerExecutor at <fix>^ and 0 at <fix>, identical every run; the wider
# net subtree (76 files) is unchanged at 4 hardcoded-secret rows on both
# revisions. The wider reachable set across the campaign's Java trees: quarkus
# holds one more instance of the shape, agroal's QuarkusNettyConnectionCache
# (`final FastThreadLocal<Acquirable> connectionCache = new
# FastThreadLocal<>()`), whose own comments state the mechanism and that the
# instance must not be created again -- reported there, 1 finding on the
# 64-file agroal subtree where the shape is the only one. solr-core, tomcat
# and protobuf mention FastThreadLocal nowhere and their finding counts are
# identical before and after (1003, 2410, 7; three runs each). The residual
# is the constructor-assigned variant: a FastThreadLocal-typed instance field
# with no initializer, built in the constructor body, holds no initializer
# for the walk to see and does not match.

test "rank1915: the combiner executor holds its task tail in a per-instance FastThreadLocal"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/io/vertx/core/net/impl/pool/CombinerExecutor.java
  expect VYQL-DOS-041
  expect_review code.UnboundedAllocationReview
  code
  ```
  package io.vertx.core.net.impl.pool;

  import io.netty.util.concurrent.FastThreadLocal;
  import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

  public class CombinerExecutor<S> implements Executor<S> {

    protected static final class InProgressTail {
      Task task;
    }

    private final AtomicInteger s = new AtomicInteger();

    private final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail> current = new FastThreadLocal<>();

    @Override
    public void submit(Action<S> action) {
      s.incrementAndGet();
      InProgressTail inProgress = current.get();
      if (inProgress == null) {
        inProgress = new InProgressTail();
        current.set(inProgress);
        current.remove();
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1915: the fixed revision makes the FastThreadLocal one per class"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/io/vertx/core/net/impl/pool/CombinerExecutor.java
  reject VYQL-DOS-041
  code
  ```
  package io.vertx.core.net.impl.pool;

  import io.netty.util.concurrent.FastThreadLocal;
  import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

  public class CombinerExecutor<S> implements Executor<S> {

    protected static final class InProgressTail<S> {
      final CombinerExecutor<S> combiner;
      Task task;

      public InProgressTail(CombinerExecutor<S> combiner, Task task) {
        this.combiner = combiner;
        this.task = task;
      }
    }

    private final AtomicInteger s = new AtomicInteger();

    private static final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail<?>> current = new FastThreadLocal<>();

    @Override
    public void submit(Action<S> action) {
      s.incrementAndGet();
      InProgressTail<S> inProgress = (InProgressTail<S>) current.get();
      if (inProgress == null) {
        inProgress = new InProgressTail<>(this, null);
        current.set(inProgress);
        current.remove();
      }
    }
  }
  ```
